## Attribution

The dork strings in `dorks/google/` are aggregated from the public sources cited
per-line in each file (see `dorks/google/README.md` for the master table). Many of
those sources are themselves redistributions of publicly indexed search queries
(such as the Exploit-DB Google Hacking Database). All query strings remain the
property of their original authors; `seer` provides no claim of authorship over
the quoted strings, only the curation, the ROI ranking, and the per-line citations.
